  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.8.44: FR0101 gives nested index loops over different collections different element names (both took `item`, the inner one shadowing the outer). FR0164 reads the target runtime: `Dictionary.Remove`/`Clear` pass from .NET Core 3.0, an indexer overwrite and `HashSet.Remove`/`Clear` from .NET 5; on .NET Framework and netstandard all of them are reported. FR0092 leaves a message a test embeds in a longer string.\n\n 0.8.43: Visual Studio extension bundles FsAutoComplete 0.85.3, whose quick fixes are titled by what they write. VS Code extension offers to install or update the `fsautocomplete` tool when Ionide's is older than 0.85.\n\n 0.8.42: FR0075 counts a window the scope does not show modally (`form.Show()`, `Application.Run form`, a method of its own that shows it) as self-active: a `use` there disposed the window on the spot (C# twin CR0060).\n\n 0.8.41: New rules FR0175 (date format `hh`/`mm`/`MM` mix-ups, fix), FR0176 (date parts from two instants, fix), FR0177 (always-true/false comparison pair), FR0178 (`.Value` in the empty branch), FR0179 (discarded immutable update), FR0180 (`Random` per call to `Random.Shared`, fix), FR0181 (specific catch around a blocking wait). FR0067 covers `Convert.To*` on a string, FR0017 `let _ = asyncCall`, FR0127 credential-named literals; reports mask credential findings. FR0049 accepts a read behind a bounded `Task.WaitAny`. Faster sweeps: files are no longer typechecked twice, and the project-wide use list is built once. `--api-changes` reads a referencing project only when its sources name the declaration.\n\n 0.8.40: FR0055 stays quiet on a catch-all with a `when` guard, on the exception or on state (`with _ when stopping -> ()`); only `when true` is still noted.\n\n 0.8.39: `--define` (and `\"defines\"` in fsharprefactor.json) defines preprocessor symbols for the whole run: every MSBuild, script and `--parse-only` compilation. A script's `#r` of the project counts only where its `#if` nesting is live; one under an undefined `#if` names the symbol to pass, and one naming a missing build is read against the project's sources.",
